# Project Style Guide (6 rules with before‑after examples)

## Rule1: State clear starting‑point prerequisites before numbered steps
❌ Before: Open the file and start editing.
✅ After: Start: Open README.md with repository edit permission.

## Rule2: Every procedure step starts with action verb
❌ Before: The user should do editing work on the intro file.
✅ After: Modify content inside README.md.

## Rule3: Keep terminology consistent; avoid vague pronouns “it”
❌ Before: Open it and finish necessary editing.
✅ After: Open README.md and modify your project introduction text.

## Rule4: Place condition clauses at sentence beginning
❌ Before: Ask administrator if you cannot edit.
✅ After: If you cannot edit, contact your repository administrator.

## Rule5: Use numbered lists for sequential task workflow
❌ Before: Open file. Then preview. Then save.
✅ After:
1. Open README.md
2. Select Preview tab
3. Commit your changes

## Rule6: Add an explicit result‑check statement after procedure
❌ Before: Check it afterwards.
✅ After: Check result: Your updated README appears on repository homepage.
